      "D1 sends a folded step as the run's work message where the step was",
      "D1 puts a resumed run's earlier steps before its first raw step",
      "D1 refuses a work message in another key order before it reaches the provider",
      "D1 refuses a work message with unescaped markup",
      "D2 runs the run's compactor in the real app-server, without tools or the run's key",
      "D3 records one usage row per provider request from Codex's six counters",
      "D4 sends the next request after a result fence slower than 8 s"
    ],
    "proves": {
      "D1": "Context composition (#896, #903) and the cache key (#912, #956, #980): every agent request carries the run's 51-character prompt_cache_key; the instructions, tools and every item before the prompt are identical in all three requests; unchanged, reasoning-dropped, folded and resumed inputs reach the provider in the composer's shape; a work message in another key order or with a raw tag is refused with \"Cloud context composition unavailable\" before it reaches the provider.",
      "D2": "The run's compactor in the real app-server (#1002, #923): two compactor requests, each with effort low, no qorpera.* tool, its own window and not the run's key; the replies come back with their usage.",
      "D3": "Usage rows (#878): Codex reports the six usage counters, including cacheWriteInputTokens; one model_request row per provider request under the model_turn attempt; the turn totals add up (170 input, 98 cached, 12 output, 1 reasoning, 182 total).",
      "D4": "A result fence slower than 8 s (#839, #914, the native half): r2's fence is held 9 s; the session still completes with 3 requests and 2 effects, r2 arrives at least 9 s after the hold began, and the held check is not c1's release check."
    }
